  "verbalization": "Myricetin appears to have a shared relationship with Calmodulin through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Myricetin acts as a target for multiple compounds, which in turn target Calmodulin. Specifically, Myricetin is linked to Peripheral myelin protein 22, which is a target of several compounds, including 5-Hydroxymethyl-9-methoxycanthin-6-one and 19-Oxo-3-beta,5,14-trihydroxy-5-beta-bufa-20,22-dienolide-3-acetate. These compounds, in turn, are connected to Calmodulin. This chain of targets implies a potential mechanism where Myricetin may influence Calmodulin through these intermediates. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a possible role for Myricetin in modulating Calmodulin activity via these molecular intermediates. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible regulatory relationship between Myricetin and Calmodulin, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
